      "post_subject": "Beam expanding...",
      "content_md": "I found this always a problem: finding a lens with a short enough focal length such as to illuminate a large object, on my small table. Best thing so far was to use 40 or 60x microscope objectives, but those tend to be expensive. I now found a cheap solution: ball lenses. If kept clean, the quality of the beam is reasonable. See:\n\n[http://www.anchoroptics.com/catalog/product.cfm?id=154](http://www.anchoroptics.com/catalog/product.cfm?id=154)\n\n[http://www.anchoroptics.com/catalog/product.cfm?id=153](http://www.anchoroptics.com/catalog/product.cfm?id=153)",
